<title>GREECE: RALLYING-ACROPOLIS RALLY FINAL POSITIONS.</title>
<headline>RALLYING-ACROPOLIS RALLY FINAL POSITIONS.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS, Greece 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading revised positions</p>
<p>in the Acropolis Rally which ended on Tuesday:</p>
<p> 1. Carlos Sainz (Spain) Ford  4 hours 56 minutes 24 seconds</p>
<p> 2. Juha Kankkunen (Finland) Ford		  4:56:41</p>
<p> 3. Tommi Makinen (Finland) Mitsubishi	   5:01:27</p>
<p> 4. Richard Burns (Britain) Mitsubishi	   5:01:31</p>
<p> 5. Thomas Radstrom (Sweden) Toyota		5:04:11</p>
<p> 6. Uwe Nittel (Germany) Mitsubishi		5:06:26</p>
<p> 7. Gregoire de Mevius (Belgium) Ford	    5:07:49</p>
<p> 8. Yukihiko Sakurai (Japan) Subaru		5:11:15</p>
<p> 9. Aris Vovos (Greece) Subaru		     5:12:05</p>
<p> 10. Leonidas Kirkos (Greece) Ford		 5:14:33</p>
<p>Briton Richard Burns picked up time penalties at the final</p>
<p>control, dropping him to fourth overall and promoting team mate</p>
<p>Tommi Makinen to third.</p>
<p>World drivers' championship standings:</p>
<p> 1. Tommi Makinen (Finland) Mitsubishi	 42</p>
<p> 2. Colin McRae (Britain) Subaru		 32</p>
<p> 3. Carlos Sainz (Spain) Ford		    28</p>
<p> 4. Pierro Liatti (Italy) Subaru		 18</p>
<p> 5. Kenneth Eriksson (Sweden) Subaru	   14</p>
<p> 6. Armin Schwarz (Germany) Ford		 11</p>
<p> 7. Richard Burns (Britain) Mitsubishi	  9</p>
<p> 8. Gilles Panizzi (France) Peugeot	     8</p>
<p>Manufacturers' standings:</p>
<p> 1. Subaru					     64</p>
<p> 2. Mitsubishi					 53</p>
<p> 3. Ford						 45</p>
